{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/15029-forum-game-forum-pantheon","id":15029,"title":"Forum Game: Forum Pantheon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-20T18:30:07-08:00","id":15029,"title":"Forum Game: Forum Pantheon","content":"So the Thread about PC Pantheons got me thinking that a cool Pantheon could be composed of the people over here, so here is a Game:<br /> <br /> Post yourself or others as a God. You can use the username as a Title or as the name or anything, post background and Associated Powers... in a similar fashion to a God writeup. Bonus points if you make it relate to your Avatar and other things you did on the forums.<br /> <br /> Also, feel free to post other related things, like Virtues, PSP (calling it Scion-Fu, but if a better name is found, I'll change it), Underworld, Godrealm, opposing Titan... anything really...<br /> <br /> I'll start:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sol'Kannar, the Man in Black, God of the Unknown</b><br /> Born from the depths of Human Fear, Sol'Kannar came into existence to ease the transition for human minds to embrace what they do not yet know and pursue it in order to understand it. The Man in Black is the one who is always a step beyond reach, looking far ahead. &quot;What lies there, where I cannot perceive?&quot;, he asks himself, but he cannot answer, for he is the one who shows the door and not the one that walks through it, the one who leads others to find what has yet to be discovered. No one understands him or his motives, for all of him is unknown, so they clad him in his black and silver robes, where his body is hidden, yet undiscovered.<br /> <br /> Even in the mortal realm, Sol'Kannar remains mysterious. He is the lone kid looking to from afar, protected from the sun under his hood. The guide who leads the explorer in his adventures of discovery. Most of the time the Man in Black takes a back role to the story unfolding, preferring to ease the transition from what is known to what will become knowledge tomorrow. To do that, he also is the unknown scientist enthusiast who supports research, the benefactor who supports the arts and exhibits them...<br /> <br /> His Scions are very rare, for it his not his nature to be close to the mortal folk. The exception is when he helps other discover their own forms of love, no matter who they are and what they want. Most children inherit his passion for the undiscovered, but prefer to take the path to do the discovery themselves instead of allowing other to pursue it. They are almost always weird children from most standards, for they wish for the yet undiscovered culture that would embrace them, leading them to lead revolutions in the field they dedicate themselves the most, be it the arts, the sciences or even politics.<br /> <br /> <b>Associated Powers:</b> Epic Appearance, Epic Perception, Darkness, Illusion, Psychopomp, Stars, Mystery, Scion-Fu<br /> <b>Favored Abilities:</b> Art, Awareness, Empathy, Investigation, Occult, Science<br /> <b>Rivals:</b> <i>(Gods who hide things, but I can't remember any right now, so.... please help?)</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T02:19:09-08:00","id":15256,"title":"","content":"<b>Gemaston, god of creativity and skalds</b><br /> Sprung forth from the primal chaos, Gemaston has always helped shape the world and give its inhabitants ideas that they would perhaps never have thought of. Among the foremost of free creativity, Gemaston is always ready to listen or to come up with something new. Not all of his ideas are brilliant, but at least they are something new that might make someone else come up with a plan that works.<br /> <br /> In the mortal realm, Gemaston appears as a fairly large human, always near laughter or merriment. He usually wears rather loose clothing and tend to appear as the funny guy at the local college or the comic book shop owner who just loves to discuss his own ideas even if they're good or not. In modern times he has appeared as a nerd shop owner, rock star and history teacher. He has also appeared as a larper, a steam punk fantast and a roleplayer.<br /> <br /> Among his Scions Gemaston favors those who come up with never before thought of solutions. He encourages them to try out new things and to never get stuck in their ways. Those of his children who survive the titan onslaught tend to do so because they are never really were people expect them to be. More than one of his Scions has stopped a potential fatal assault from the titans by simply 'happening' to be there because of some crazy scheme.<br /> <br /> <b>Associated Powers:</b> Epic Charisma, Epic Wits, Industry, Illusion, Scion-Fu. Sky<br /> <b>Favored Abilities:</b> Academics, Art, Craft, Integrity, Presence, Science<br /> <b>Rivals:</b> <i>Hephaistos, Hermes, Loki, Ptah, Set</i>[/QUOTE]<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T08:08:50-08:00","id":15389,"title":"","content":"<b>Iryklathagra, God of Mechanics</b><br /> Born the child of a human and some unknown god, he was adopted by Athena who paid an unusually high price for the right to do so. These days, Iryklathagra has ascended to the ranks of lower divinity and spends much of his time hunched over countless spreadsheets and mathematical theorems. He is driven by obsessive compulsive need to dissect each and every system presented to him into its component parts. Every weakness is discovered, every exploit is noted, and every potential abuse is explored with sadistic glee.<br /> <br /> Athena often presents him with various plans so that he can discover and report flaws. He pines after Aphrodite like all men, but suspects that he might get some kind of disease if he ever succeeded in such a conquest. Unfortunately for mortals like he used to be, Iryklathagra often runs mechanical experiments upon large groups of them under the guise of Roleplaying Games. Each player is nothing more than a tormented cog in the great machine, and they emerge from the experience permanently scarred.<br /> <br /> <b>Associated Powers:</b> Epic Charisma, Epic Intelligence, Epic Wits, Arete, Justice, Prophecy<br /> <b>Favored Abilities:</b> Academics, Empathy, Investigation, Occult, Politics, Science<br /> <b>Rivals:</b> <i>JSR</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 11-21-2013, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T08:25:35-08:00","id":15396,"title":"","content":"/<b>Darksol Aeternium</b>, the reflection on the void<br /> A being called forth from the void by the stirrings of human imagination. One who is spurred to action by the latent emptiness of the human soul, and motivated to fill it. Whether inspiring fear, creativity, or contemplation, his voice echoes from the nether reaches which all souls originate. He is a sibilant echo of the primal demiurgic impulse which began the creation of all. He is the space between the stars that grants them their distinction, the darkness that lets light shine, and the shadows that give perspective. Scholars in the divine wonder fi this creature is truly a god or merely a defected titan.<br /> <br /> It is rare to find him in the mortal world per se, it's far more likely to have a direct encounter with him in ones dreams. Mortals tend not to be perceptive enough to properly interpret what signs and portents he would send them in the waking world. If he must appear in the mortal world it is rarely as anything even vaguely anthropomorphic.<br /> <br /> The few scions he has are chosen precisely for their attention to the abstract and greater than average insight. He charges them to motivate humankind to realize its potential and rise beyond the petty materialism inherent in the species. Against the titans his children exploit the friction between each overtitan faction and orchestrate internal strife that leads to their ultimate downfall.<br /> <br /> <b>Associated Powers</b>: Epic Intelligence, Epic Manipulation, Darkness, Stars, Illusion, Guardian, Moon, Scion-Fu<br /> <b>Favored Abilities</b>: Academics, Integrity, Investigation, Politics, Presence, Stealth<br /> <b>Rivals</b>: Morpheus, Ratri, Nyarlathotep","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T14:07:03-08:00","id":15619,"title":"","content":"<b>Cuauhocelotl </b>(&quot;Eagle-jaguar&quot;)<br /> <br /> A child of some unknown foreign deity, the Scion now known as Cuauhocelotl (an approximation of his mortal name, based on a creature comprised of both eagle and large cat) became adopted by the Aztec Pantheon due to his passion towards studying their history and advancing their reputation throughout the world. He serves them now in a number of capacities, protecting the wilds and creatures of Central America, unearthing ancient knowledge buried deep within the earth, gaining knowledge for the pantheon through study of old bones, and guiding young Scions in the traditions of their parents.<br /> <br /> Found frequently in the world, often as a university professor, an enthusiastic birdwatcher, a game warden, a participant in archaeological digs, a tour guide at museums and historical sites, or even just a man walking his dog through a wooded area. Cuauhocelotl typically enthralled in whatever he's doing, often surrounded by animals and conveys his passion for knowledge and nature with an infectious eagerness. Woe to all who might shun or belittle his quest for knowledge, or worse, try to undermine his goals to preserve animals. Those people often find themselves chosen by Cuauhocelotl as the next candidate for his sacrificial altars.<br /> <br /> There are scant few Scions of Cuauhocelotl, he's typically more engrossed in his projects to sire them. He only chooses those who share his passions and would aid him in his goals. Those few he does choose, however, count among the most heavily schooled Scions you'd ever find<br /> <br /> <b>Associated Powers</b>: Animal (Jaguar, Golden Retriever), Death, Earth, Fertility, Epic Intelligence, Epic Perception, Guardian, Itztli, Mystery<br /> <b>Favored Abilities</b>: Academics, Animal Ken, Investigation, Occult, Science, Survival<br /> <b>Rivals</b>: Anyone who disseminates misinformation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T11:24:24-08:00","id":16197,"title":"","content":"<b>The Mad Man</b><br /> The Mad Man, enigmatically referred to either as &quot;The Mad Man&quot; or any number of other similar names, is the god of obscurity, enigmatic mysteries and bizarre things. He appears in some places, not doing anything important, at other times he is a kind but very eccentric man, and yet at other times he can cause chaos, madness and rage in others. His behavior is erratic and unpredictable. As said before, he can be quite kind and generous, OR malicious. It is difficult to tell if he has a method to his madness, or if he's just insane. He is seen as a deity of chaos, magic, illusion, and for some, obscure and cosmic knowledge. Some speculate that he simply learned too much about the universe to stay mentally stable. He occasionally gives great insight into the workings of the universe and warns others of danger. For others, he occasionally curses, not out of spite, but out of insanity, believing reality to be different than it is. <br /> <br /> <b>Associated Purviews</b>: Magic, Illusion, Psychopomp, Mystery, Prophecy, Chaos<br /> <b>Favored Attributes</b>: Manipulation, Perception, Intelligence<br /> <b>Favored Abilities</b>: Occult, Larceny, Stealth, Command, Academics, Presence<br /> <b>Rivals</b>: Cuauhocelotl (accidental spread of misinformation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), Loki, Eshu, Space Battles, Role Player Guild<br /> <br /> <b>The Mad Man And Space Battles</b><br /> The Mad Man frequently appeared in the past at a message board called Space Battles. In it, he would frequently argue and debate with bigoted Anti-Religionists. The records of his exact debates and arguments with them have not been found, but what has been remembered is that he had adopted many different names. He normally won debates he had with the members there, but occasionally lost when his less than perfect grammar made him appear to be saying what he wasn't saying. Because he consistently won his arguments there, and he inconveniently made a few grammar slips, he was cast out as a racist. <br /> <br /> <b>The Mad Man And Role Player Guild </b><br /> In this message board he was falsely accused of advocating genocide.by the moderators, and those who kiss their ass. He was on the message board for many years without much of an incident but was cast out because a couple of moderators decided to be assholes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/952-exdeath","name":"ExDeath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar952_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T17:54:18-08:00","id":16366,"title":"","content":"Enter the <b>Fires of Darklight</b>, aka &quot;Shadowflame&quot; who has dusted himself off through the aeons of time because of the constant trend in fantasy that's bothering the shit out of him with this ongoing idea of &quot;shadow&quot; equating with &quot;darkness.&quot;<br /> He's all about equilibrium; two polar opposing forces with a third for balance, and because of that he's become his own trinity, running with three concepts that encompass three purviews each.<br /> <br /> But rather than run with that, I'll keep it in Scion:<br /> <br /> <b>A</b><b>ssociated Purviews</b>: Moon, Darkness, Magic, Mystery, Sun, Fire, Epic Wits, Epic Strength, Epic Dexterity, Epic Stamina, Epic Perception, Epic Intelligence, Animal (panther, owl, squirrel)<br /> <br /> <b>Favored Abilities: </b>Academics, Awareness, Occult, Stealth, Brawl, Melee, Investigation<br /> He's pretty much a loner. Toyed with the idea of becoming Godking of magical beasts for a while since he thinks they always get the short end of fate, but realizes that there are a lot of titan business going on with a lot of them, so he maintains a distance. He hates bullies however, so if he sees a god pulling the wings of the great phoenix for a little bit of fun (<i>Hey! They'll grow back. What's the big deal</i>?) he'll likely intervene with extreme prejudice.<br /> He thinks he's head over heels in love with Ratri, and has a friendly rivalry with Agni.<br /> <br /> <b>Rivals</b>: Tezcatlipoca, Odin, Set, Amaterasu<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">I originally had something very different. However it was for a whole different game than this, and the deity I created was a great deal bigger..and the concepts/ideas were very very different.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T19:46:20-08:00","id":16433,"title":"","content":"<b>Ayndais, Goddess of Troubles</b><br /> The concept of being careful what you wished for is one that this goddess happily abides by. Too often she'll check in with her various cults of worshipers and overhear them speaking of how a situation could go horribly wrong. She is all too happy to prove them right, that it could go that wrong, and then happily listens to the lamentations of the poor, unfortunate souls caught up in the aftermath.<br /> <br /> She's often found in the world browsing through various forms of media to pick up tricks and tribulations to test out on her worshipers. Forums, libraries, and college classrooms are her haunting grounds. One creates sacrifices to keep her evil ideas of mischief from coming true, but then again... most of her followers are masochists.<br /> <br /> <b>Associated Powers: </b>Manipulation, Wits, Moon, Artistry, Enech<br /> <b>Favored Abilities: </b>Academics, Art, Empathy, Investigation, Occult, Politics<br /> <b>Rivals: </b>Iryklathagra","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T20:27:59-08:00","id":16441,"title":"","content":"<b>The Watching Man, God of Tales</b><br /> The keeper of stories in all forms. From great epics, encompassing civilizations, to lesser stories, the simple lives of individuals. He ever watches, and remembers the important, and 'unimportant' things. For if he doesn't, who will? With the tales, in their countless numbers, the patterns are observed, and with careful consideration, more heroes and deeds are spun for budding tales. A thousand heroes with different faces.<br /> <br /> Cults and worshipers record and remember those who have no others to remember them, and they gather stories from fellow mortals before their deeds are lost to death, and time. Sacrifices of secrets carved into great stones, scribed into dusty pages, and cut into sticks. Although the last is lest likely to be noticed or met with much more then ire.<br /> <br /> <b>Associated Powers</b>: Epic Charisma, Epic Intelligence, Magic, Mystery, Enech<br /> <b>Favored Abilities</b>: Academics, Awareness, Empathy, Occult, Politics, Stealth<br /> <b>Enemies</b>: Cernunnos","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T20:46:08-08:00","id":16446,"title":"","content":"<b>Leliel, Angel of Fantasy</b><br /> <br /> One of the major victories of the Order of Divine Glory, Leliel is the fusion of several dead gods of dream and magic into a single, God-level archangel, created by the collective beliefs of a generation of third-world citizens who were given an Order-backed college education fund and investment, and their dreams of prosperity for their nations given the divine corpses a conceptual form to reorganize themselves into. Sometimes described as a &quot;brilliant idiot&quot;, Leliel embodies the power of the night sky to inspire and the metaphorical heights that properly applied dreams can achieve, and upon his birth Leliel wasted no time in dancing through the dreams of mortals, inspiring them to ever greater heights...all for the glory of God, of course.<br /> <br /> Truth is, while Fate has made him an angel of the Lord, Leliel is secretly an agnostic-he honestly doesn't know if there is truly something worthy of being called a God in the Judeo-Christian sense of the term, or even if there will be (nor does he want a definite answer-navel gazing about it is too much fun). He is also a complete klutz and cannot keep more than one than one train of thought stable at a time, regularly forgetting what precisely he was doing in the middle of it due to dedicating part of his brain to his own little world. He's quite capable of great philosophical insights and lateral thinking, however, it's just that he is <i>terrible</i> at applying his mind to more concrete matters. He's also an adept violinist, and a soft sonata usually follows him around to announce his presence (though he prefers rock).<br /> <br /> <b>A</b><b>ssociated Purviews: </b>Animal (Birds and dogs), Chaos, Epic Charisma, Epic Intelligence, Epic Wits, Illusion, Magic, Moon, Mystery, Scion-Fu, Sky, Stars<br /> <br /> <b>Favored Abilities:</b> Academics, Art, Investigation, Occult, Science, Presence<br /> <br /> <b>Rivals:</b> As a young God and a representative of a possible future with only One True God (tm), most of the others are quite nervous about Leliel. For his part, he could care less, preferring to inspire without contempt or malice. He absolutely <i>despises</i> Aten, however, and is a happy ally of the Pesedjet because of it, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 11-22-2013, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T00:33:51-08:00","id":16507,"title":"","content":"<b>Rian mac Phoebus, Loremaker</b><br /> <br /> Child of Apollo and Airmed, Rian is a maker of worlds, tinkering in the 'empty' spaces between Godrealms to create Terra Incognitae, and then peopling them with beings of many kinds. Once he has tamed a raw planet sufficiently and breathed life into its oceans, planted forests and grasslands and sculpted rivers and mountains, forming beasts and magic creatures and people, gifting them with languages and magic, he searches among the younger gods and scions to find appropriate caretakers. His greatest accomplishment thus far has been the world taerth, cared for by Tiamat the Mother Dragon and all her Scions, lit by the three moons and sheltering vestiges of great alfar and svartalfar kingdoms. <br /> <br /> Rian grew to adulthood in the shadow of the Teotl and the Hero Twins of the Dine, has flown the world twice in his wanderings, drank the oceans of east and west, made and buried many tongues and scripts, and from his breath and mind and hands bore many strange and wondrous beings. He has grown world trees from stolen shoots of Yggdrasil, parted the veil behind the stars, and flown on the back of leviathan. Twin suns are his protectors; one moment they are wolves, then lions, rays in the ocean or otters, crocodiles, or ravens. In every form they guard his steps from the ravenous Void. <br /> <br /> <b>Associated Purviews:</b> Stamina, Charisma, Intelligence; Animal, Artistry, Creation, Earth, Fertility, Magic, Prophecy, Sun, Sky, Water<br /> <br /> <b>Favored Abilities: </b>Academics, Art, Brawl, Empathy, Integrity, Occult<br /> <br /> Taerth: <a href=\"http://jrhyder.deviantart.com/art/Taerth-Rework-172960441\" target=\"_blank\">http://jrhyder.deviantart.com/art/Ta...work-172960441</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/911-phoebuslore","name":"phoebuslore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar911_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}